# BPB Website — skeletons

## When to use

- Any section that waits on Supabase (or other async) before showing real content
- Prefer skeletons over a lone “Loading…” line when the final layout is known
- Errors / empty states stay plain status text — do not leave a skeleton up after failure
- **Nav:** `#site-nav` may ship with skeleton markup in HTML; `initNav()` keeps it until shelf/logo images load, then swaps in the real header (`navSkeletonHtml()` in `js/shared/nav.js`)

## Shared primitives

- JS: `js/shared/skeleton.js` — `skelBar()`, `skelBlock()`, `skelRegion()`
- CSS: `js/shared/skeleton.css` (imported from `css/shared.css`)
- Classes: `.bpb-skel`, `.bpb-skel--bar`, `.bpb-skel--block`, `.bpb-skel-region`

Compose **page-specific** skeleton markup that mirrors the real section layout; do not invent a second generic “card skeleton” system unless several pages share the same shape.

## Habits

- Paint the skeleton **immediately** on init (before `await`)
- Match real sizing (aspect-ratio, track padding, grid) so content does not jump
- Parchment-tinted shimmer only — no gray SaaS bone UI, no purple pulse
- Honor `prefers-reduced-motion` (already in shared CSS)
- Mark busy: `skelRegion(..., { label: '…' })` → `aria-busy` + `role="status"`
- Keep helpers in `js/shared/`; section-specific skeleton HTML stays in that page module

## Example

```js
import { skelBar, skelBlock, skelRegion } from '../../shared/skeleton.js';

host.innerHTML = skelRegion(
  `<div class="my-card">${skelBlock()}${skelBar({ width: '70%' })}</div>`,
  { label: 'Loading builds' },
);
// …await fetch…
host.innerHTML = realHtml;
```
